T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A parallel-plate circular capacitor has plates of radius R = 100 mm) Tj
T*
(separated by distance d = 2.0 mm in air \(epsilon_0 = 8.854 * 10^-12 F/m\). It is charged) Tj
T*
(by an AC voltage V\(t\) = 230 * sqrt\(2\) * sin\(100 * pi * t\) Volts \(50 Hz\). Calculate: \(1\)) Tj
T*
(Capacitance C, \(2\) Conduction current i_c entering the plates, \(3\) Displacement current) Tj
T*
(density J_d between the plates, \(4\) Magnetic field B at radius r = 50 mm from central) Tj
T*
(axis.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Capacitance C:) Tj
T*
(Area A = pi * R^2 = pi * \(0.10\)^2 = 0.031416 m^2.) Tj
T*
(C = \(epsilon_0 * A\) / d = \(8.854 * 10^-12 * 0.031416\) / 0.002 = 1.3908 * 10^-10 F =) Tj
T*
(139.08 pF.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Conduction Current i_c\(t\):) Tj
T*
(i_c\(t\) = C * \(dV/dt\) = C * [ 230 * sqrt\(2\) * \(100 * pi\) * cos\(100 * pi * t\) ].) Tj
T*
(Peak conduction current: I_c_peak = 1.3908 * 10^-10 * 325.27 * 314.16 = 1.421 * 10^-5 A) Tj
T*
(= 14.21 microamps.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Displacement Current Density J_d:) Tj
T*
(Electric field between plates: E\(t\) = V\(t\) / d.) Tj
T*
(J_d = epsilon_0 * \(dE/dt\) = \(epsilon_0 / d\) * \(dV/dt\) = \(C / A\) * \(dV/dt\) = i_c\(t\) / A.) Tj
T*
(Peak J_d = I_c_peak / A = 1.421 * 10^-5 A / 0.031416 m^2 = 4.523 * 10^-4 A/m^2 \(452.3) Tj
T*
(microamps/m^2\).) Tj
T*
(Total displacement current i_d = J_d * A = I_c_peak = 14.21 microamps \(Displacement) Tj
T*
(current matches conduction current identically!\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Magnetic field B at radius r = 50 mm \(r < R\):) Tj
T*
