(Problem Context: In marine civil engineering, ground-penetrating radar \(GPR\) operates at) Tj
T*
(frequency f = 25 MHz in seawater \(relative permittivity epsilon_r = 81, permeability mu) Tj
T*
(= mu_0 = 4*pi*10^-7 H/m, conductivity sigma = 4.0 S/m\). Calculate: \(1\) Conduction to) Tj
T*
(displacement current ratio sigma / \(omega * epsilon\), \(2\) Skin depth delta, \(3\) Distance) Tj
T*
(at which wave power drops by 40 dB.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Conduction to Displacement Current Ratio:) Tj
T*
(Angular frequency: omega = 2 * pi * f = 2 * pi * 25 * 10^6 = 1.5708 * 10^8 rad/s.) Tj
T*
(epsilon = epsilon_r * epsilon_0 = 81 * 8.854 * 10^-12 = 7.1717 * 10^-10 F/m.) Tj
T*
(omega * epsilon = 1.5708 * 10^8 * 7.1717 * 10^-10 = 0.1126 S/m.) Tj
T*
(Ratio = sigma / \(omega * epsilon\) = 4.0 / 0.1126 = 35.51 >> 1 => Behaves as a good) Tj
T*
(conductor.) Tj
T*
